loat-kernels/issues/17/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/17/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/17/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/statuses/eff6e0fdc66f447de926d6544a14b3a92afef737"}},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/16","id":4954222300,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-E3Y88AAAABJ0tu3A","html_url":"https://github.com/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pull/16","diff_url":"https://github.com/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pull/16.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pull/16.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/issues/16","number":16,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Score the full entry on a drawn suite of inputs, behind GATE_FULL_SUITE","user":{"login":"rob-dendrite","id":289653679,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUPDrw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289653679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite","html_url":"https://github.com/rob-dendrite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rob-dendrite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What and why\n\nThe full entry is timed on twelve fixed, public input classes: one exponent band, one `sum` length (1000) and one `bmm` shape (50×100×50). NaN, infinities and subnormal inputs are never timed, and the `mul` classes contain no zeros. A kernel can therefore win with a fast path whose slow fallback the benchmark never pays for.\n\nWith `GATE_FULL_SUITE` set, the full entry is instead timed on a fresh plan of cases drawn per run from a **suite**. Without the setting, nothing changes. Practice boards are unchanged either way.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **`benchmark_suite.py`**:\n  - loads and validates a suite: *groups* of value *families* with parameter ranges, kernel weights, work per kernel, and size distributions;\n  - draws a plan from the seed, with each group's cases per kernel plus one untimed raw-bits checksum case per kernel;\n  - scores it. A cell (kernel × group) is the geometric mean of its cases' ratios, and the headline is the weighted geometric mean of the cells, each kernel weighted equally. Time no longer decides how much a kind of input counts.\n- **`lean/bench/BenchSuite.lean`** builds the operands from SplitMix64 counter streams:\n  - uniform or normal-like magnitudes;\n  - zeros, alone or in runs: `+0`, `-0`, signed, or leaked tiny values;\n  - subnormal blocks;\n  - specials (±∞, NaN payloads, ±max, subnormals, ±0) at a rate, on a stride, in bursts or at row edges;\n  - fractions reduced to bf16, fp16 or fewer bits;\n  - codebooks and per-block scales;\n  - for `add` and `mul`, a second operand tied to the first: equal, negated, cancelling, near, constant, identity, or offset by binades.\n\n  `MainFull` runs it when `BENCH_PLAN` is set.\n- **`gate.py`**: draws the plan, passes it in `BENCH_PLAN`, and requires every case's row and matching checksums.\n  - The verdict publishes results: per-cell ratios in `classes`, and every case's round times under its cell in `suite`. It never includes the plan, so a private suite's contents stay private.\n  - The suite file's hash enters the verifier fingerprint.\n- **Admission** has its own policy for suite evidence, `suite-cell-bootstrap-v1`, so legacy decisions keep their seeds:\n  - the bootstrap resamples both rounds and cases within each cell;\n  - a new outcome, `regressed`, refuses any entry with a cell more than 5% slower than the champion (`REGRESSION_GUARD`).\n\n  The worker and the weight setter both read the evidence from the stored report. No schema change.\n- **`suites/public-v2.json`**: the public suite (7 groups, 80 cases per run) for local tuning.\n- **Docs**: BENCHMARKING (suite scoring), MANUAL, OPERATIONS (switching a board to a private suite), `.env.example`.\n\n## Checks run locally\n\n- `ruff check .` and `ruff format --check .`: clean.\n- `pytest -q -m \"not slow\"` against Postgres 17: 265 passed, 3 skipped (no bwrap sandbox on that host). The 29 new tests cover:\n  - plans: reproducibility, coverage, budgets, size spread, refusing broken suites;\n  - gate scoring with a fake bench: cell maths, the plan kept out of the verdict, missing cases, checksum mismatches, practice slots ignoring the suite;\n  - suite admission: qualifies, regressed, lucky-case not-significant, thin evidence, reproducibility;\n  - worker and weight setter reaching the same decision from a real verdict.\n- **Real binaries.** `lake build benchFull` ran for the shipped incumbent and three PROD-era kernels, and all four suites and legacy ran end to end with checksums agreeing. I dumped the generated operands and checked them against every family's parameters.\n- **Noise.** Baseline against itself scores within ±0.3% of 1.00 on every suite at 5 rounds.\n- **Cost.** A baseline bench process takes about 4.9 s on the public suite, against 3.3 s on legacy.\n- **Not run:** the slow `-m slow` gate test and `selftest.py`, which need a bwrap sandbox.\n\n## Deploy / operator steps\n\nNone while `GATE_FULL_SUITE` is unset. To score a board on a suite, see OPERATIONS.md, \"Scoring the full board on a private suite\":\n- keep the file outside the checkout, mode 0600;\n- raise `GATE_BUDGET_SECONDS` and `VERIFY_TOTAL_TIMEOUT`;\n- deploy conjectures-io/conjectures-validator#149 first, so `regressed` shows on the boards;\n- decide what happens to the current champion.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-21T15:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T13:26:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T13:26:37Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12566616782,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU-E3Y88AAAAC7Qdazg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/16/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/16/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/issues/16/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-float-kernels/statuses/2b85f9c28e7440b9277bbb9ceb9366620ceec12a","head":{"label":"conjectures-io:feat/benchmark-suite-v2","ref":"feat/benchmark-suite-v2","sha":"2b85f9c